      "shortId": "A7JKV",
      "priority": 2,
      "shortName": "bind-any-action-by-name",
      "title": "Let config bind ANY action by name, contributed ones included",
      "status": "done",
      "description": "keybindings.default.toml and the user's keybindings only speak to built-in `WmAction`s today. The registry is already keyed by name, so this is a lookup, not a new mechanism. Same syntax as a built-in — a user should not need to know whether an action is built in or contributed.\n\n---\n**Completion summary:**\nClosed 2026-08-04 by a reconciliation pass, not by new work — **it was delivered by F003/P085 and the plugin-04 G3 change**, and the board was stale.\n\n`action_ref_from_config` (`heca/src/app/registry.rs:32`) resolves a config binding by name: built-in with args → `ActionRef::Builtin`, bare built-in → `ActionRef::Builtin`, and **anything else → `ActionRef::Dynamic(intent)`**, carrying the `args` table as `PropValue::Text`. The comment at `registry.rs:21` states the rule: \"Anything else ⇒ `ActionRef::Dynamic` — **not an error** (plugin-04 G3). Config is loaded before providers activate\", so a name that does not exist yet resolves at **press** time.\n\nThat is exactly what this task asked for: same syntax as a built-in, a lookup rather than a new mechanism, and a user who never has to know whether an action is built in or contributed.",
