    {
      "id": "58a4843a-f15c-4313-86a4-e694f82f8921",
      "phaseId": "2219cca3-9ed4-4708-9e4c-bc480faad753",
      "number": 324,
      "shortId": "NEETL",
      "priority": 3,
      "shortName": "palette-lists-contributed",
      "title": "Command palette lists contributed actions",
      "status": "done",
      "description": "`ActionCatalog::describe_all()` already returns `ActionInfo` (serde) with label, icon and category — everything a palette needs. The palette does not read it. Feed it from there so contributed actions are listed, searchable and runnable.\n\n---\n**Completion summary:**\nClosed 2026-08-04 by a reconciliation pass — **delivered by P085(F003)/T358**, which was written after this task was filed and went further than it asked.\n\n`heca/src/chrome/palette.rs::entries` builds every row from `catalog.all()`, so a contributed action is listed with its label, description, icon (via `catalog.icon`, which falls back to the category's glyph so no row is blank) and its bindings. It is searchable through the shared `SearchModel` like any other row.\n\nT358 also solved the part this task did not anticipate: a contributed action usually declares `ActionPolicy::ContainerFocused`, so merely *listing* it would produce an entry that is refused when chosen. `InteractionIntent::FocusContainerThenAction` focuses the owning placement first and then performs, which satisfies the policy instead of bypassing it. Rows are labelled with the owning component's title (`\"Containers › Restart Container\"`), and actions with a **required** argument are not offered at all — arity, read off the `args` every action declares.\n\nNote this task had earlier been raised as a possible cancellation; it is closed as **done**, not cancelled, because the capability exists and is shipped.",
      "notes": "",
      "statusLog": [],
      "decisions": [],
      "acceptedDecisions": [],
