    {
      "id": "dcda3d13-0225-42e5-b5bf-d39d4896d580",
      "phaseId": "2219cca3-9ed4-4708-9e4c-bc480faad753",
      "number": 334,
      "shortId": "4LDUG",
      "priority": 1,
      "shortName": "read-default-binding",
      "title": "Offer ActionMeta.default_binding to the keymap on registration",
      "status": "canceled",
      "description": "`ActionMeta` already carries `default_binding` (heca/src/actions.rs) and nothing reads it, so registering an action never makes a key work. Read it at `register_dynamic` time and offer it to the keymap. Never hardcode — it goes through `KeymapRegistry` like everything else.",
      "notes": "",
      "statusLog": [
        {
          "id": "dcda3d13-0225-42e5-b5bf-d39d4896d580-check-001-planned-canceled",
          "date": "2026-08-04T19:36:06.896Z",
          "fromStatus": "planned",
          "toStatus": "canceled",
          "title": "Cancelled by Antonio 2026-08-04, on the reconciliation pass. The task asks to read `ActionMeta.default_binding` at registration and offer it to the keymap — but **that field no longer exists**. It was deliberately deleted because it \"held a *second* copy of every key already in `keybindings.default.toml` — one nothing compared against, so the two could drift silently\" (`heca/src/keymap.rs:139`, `heca/src/providers/mod.rs:206`). Executing this task as written would resurrect exactly what was removed on purpose.",
          "description": "Cancelled by Antonio 2026-08-04, on the reconciliation pass. The task asks to read `ActionMeta.default_binding` at registration and offer it to the keymap — but **that field no longer exists**. It was deliberately deleted because it \"held a *second* copy of every key already in `keybindings.default.toml` — one nothing compared against, so the two could drift silently\" (`heca/src/keymap.rs:139`, `heca/src/providers/mod.rs:206`). Executing this task as written would resurrect exactly what was removed on purpose.\n\nIts goal — \"registering an action makes a key work\" — is delivered instead by **F003/P086/T366**: `Provider::keybindings() -> Vec<(String, String)>` is the plugin path, consumed by `bind_provider_keybindings` (`heca/src/providers/actions.rs:86`) at mount **and after a reload** (a reload rebuilds the layers from a file that knows nothing about a plugin mounted afterwards, so without the second call every plugin key would silently unbind). Core components write their keys in `keybindings.default.toml` under `[[keys.component]]` instead, where `--keys-show` finds them and the user edits them in one place.\n\nReplaced, not dropped."
        }
      ],
      "decisions": [],
      "acceptedDecisions": [],
      "checklist": [
